  Corsairs of Meridian                                 ���������   � �߲��
                                                           ���    � ���� ���
  A Scenario for 1-2 Players by George Moromisato       �     � � � �������
  Difficulty: Beginner       Length: 50+ years            �   � � � �������


NEWPAGE

 The collapse came without warning. One century the sector thrived; the next,
 it burned. The Spinward Alliance's fall scattered refugees across a dozen
 systems, and with them came desperation, disease, and the slow death of
 trade. By 3651, the Charlatt sector was a graveyard of broken ships and
 abandoned stations.

 This scenario recreates the Charlatt sector in the years following the
 collapse. Once a prosperous mining region on the edge of the Tyreemean Arm,
 it survived the Alliance's tyranny only to drown in the chaos that followed.
 When the sector capital was destroyed in 3428, the power vacuum gave rise
 to the Corsairs of Meridian -- a pirate fleet that preyed on the weak and
 grew fat on the wreckage of civilization.

NEWPAGE

 It is 3451. The surviving worlds have turned inward, hoarding what little
 they have. You must rebuild the trade networks that once made this sector
 rich. You must unite the scattered colonies and bring order to a region
 ruled by fear. And you must hunt down Meridian itself -- the heart of the
 pirate empire, and the only power that can stop you.

 But Meridian will not wait. Every year you spend building, they grow stronger.
 Every world you hesitate to claim, they claim instead. The clock is running,
 and the corsairs are watching.

ENDTEXT

BEGINDESCRIPTION

